# Kindle the Inner Flame (CR 707.2, 707.9a, 603.2): Bot1 casts Regathan Firecat (4/1) and then Kindle targeting it. The
# token copy has haste, so it attacks the turn it is made and Bot2 takes 4; it is sacrificed at the beginning of the end step
# by the ability the copy's exception gives it. The Firecat stays and Kindle is in the graveyard.
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus x3
Regathan Firecat
Kindle the Inner Flame
Mountain x2
Mountain x10
[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Regathan Firecat.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Kindle the Inner Flame.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Regathan Firecat)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Regathan Firecat#2.Token = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Regathan Firecat#2.Keywords = Haste
! Bot1.Attack(Regathan Firecat#1 > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Regathan Firecat#2 > Bot2)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 16
[T2 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot1.Battlefield = Regathan Firecat
Bot1.Graveyard = Kindle the Inner Flame; Black Lotus; Black Lotus; Black Lotus
